        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-17T00:56:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The way this is coded right now, if the CRC is bad, every call will re-read the entire CBI, and error out before here.  So every call will be slow.\n\nSeems like there are 4 states:\n- Uninitialized\n- I2C read errors (can\u0027t get at the data)\n- Read data, but invalid contents (bad checksum, version, or crc)\n- Valid data\n\nOnly need to read from I2C if it\u0027s uninitialized.  If we\u0027re worried about I2C read errors, the first attempt should make retries, but after that subsequent calls to read_board_info() would know there\u0027s a hardware problem and wouldn\u0027t try to read.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 86,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 86,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "8a6c31a5ae0092424d4dd26761062d0be8a99466",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
